<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Rimfolk's ways to play (the player's request, 12 November 2026; docs/storytellers-proposals.md): eight storytellers,
    each named for what it does, with no character and no portrait (a plain plate with its name, Tools/make_storyteller_plates.py).
    Each is a whole storyteller with the game's own difficulty settings: the game's parts (BaseStoryteller's endgame and
    DLC quests, then its own threats, sickness, traders, visitors, caravans and quests), Rimfolk's own parts where the
    game's can't say the way (Source/ColonyCouncil/Story/StoryComps.cs), and Rimfolk's levers on its own happenings
    (StoryWayExtension, Source/ColonyCouncil/Story/StoryDirection.cs). The same levers lean any storyteller through the
    story direction setting. Harm keeps the game's own rate: each way's threats come at the classic storyteller's pace or
    less over a year or an arc, and its levers on what hurts are never above 1.
  -->

  <!-- 1. The Long Road: the world calls the colony out. Threats at home about three quarters of the classic pace; more on the road. -->
  <StorytellerDef ParentName="BaseStoryteller">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Story_LongRoad</defName>
    <label>The Long Road</label>
    <description>The world calls the colony out. Fewer raids come to the gate, about three quarters of the classic pace, and more of the story waits in the region: letters asking for help, favours called in, camps on the land, missions and quests, travellers on the road. Ambushes and chance meetings follow the colony's caravans more than its walls.\n\nFor a game of journeys and the region map.\n\nIt leans toward these, never away from anything: every kind of event can still come.</description>
    <portraitLarge>ColonyCouncil/Storytellers/LongRoad</portraitLarge>
    <portraitTiny>ColonyCouncil/Storytellers/LongRoadTiny</portraitTiny>
    <listOrder>61</listOrder>
    <comps>
      <li Class="StorytellerCompProperties_ClassicIntro"/>
      <!-- Home threats: the classic cycle with longer quiet spells -->
      <li Class="StorytellerCompProperties_OnOffCycle">
        <category>ThreatBig</category>
        <minDaysPassed>11.0</minDaysPassed>
        <onDays>4.6</onDays>
        <offDays>9.4</offDays>
        <minSpacingDays>1.9</minSpacingDays>
        <numIncidentsRange>1~2</numIncidentsRange>
        <forceRaidEnemyBeforeDaysPassed>20</forceRaidEnemyBeforeDaysPassed>
        <disallowedTargetTags>
          <li>Map_RaidBeacon</li>
        </disallowedTargetTags>
      </li>
      <li Class="StorytellerCompProperties_ThreatsGenerator">
