  <!-- 3. The Turning Year: the calendar decides. Threats and sickness by the season, about the classic pace over a year. -->
  <StorytellerDef ParentName="BaseStoryteller">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Story_TurningYear</defName>
    <label>The Turning Year</label>
    <description>The calendar decides. Quiet springs, with sickness coming with the thaw; growing summers of heat waves and blight; trade and camps in autumn, when the harvest is in; then a hard winter, its cold snaps and the hungry raids of late winter. Every year has the same shape and different contents, so the colony can plan for its seasons. Over a year the threats and the sickness come about as often as the classic pace.\n\nFor a game of fields, stores and the colony's calendar.\n\nIt leans toward these, never away from anything: every kind of event can still come.</description>
    <portraitLarge>ColonyCouncil/Storytellers/TurningYear</portraitLarge>
    <portraitTiny>ColonyCouncil/Storytellers/TurningYearTiny</portraitTiny>
