  <!-- 4. What You Sow: the colony's deeds decide. Raids from the classic pace (cruel) down to two thirds of it (kind), never more. -->
  <StorytellerDef ParentName="BaseStoryteller">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Story_WhatYouSow</defName>
    <label>What You Sow</label>
    <description>The colony's deeds decide, as the peoples remember them. Cruelty draws raiders with a grievance at the classic pace, and the roads thin: a quarter of the traders, visitors and friends in a fight still come. Kindness spares the colony a third of the raids and brings traders, visitors and friends at the gate in a fight. Nothing is told: the world simply answers, and its peoples remember longer.\n\nFor a game where how the colony treats others matters.\n\nIt leans toward these, never away from anything: every kind of event can still come.</description>
